※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4646

※ A generic function calling another with its own type parameters knows of
※ those types only what its own requirements say, so every requirement of the
※ one it calls has to follow from them.  What a type must support reaches the
※ signature a caller reads, up the whole chain.

fn bigger(a: T', b: T') → T' pre(T' ⌈ T' → T'):
    a ⌈ b

fn either(a: T', b: T') → T':
    bigger(a, b)

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
